#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The traders weigh their silver on small scales: a broken piece of a bracelet buys as much as a "
"coin of the same weight."
msgstr ""
"I mercanti pesano l'argento su piccole bilance: un pezzo rotto di un braccialetto compra quanto "
"una moneta dello stesso peso."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "The combs of antler are so precious that people are buried with them."
msgstr "I pettini di corno sono così preziosi che la gente viene sepolta insieme a loro."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "The vikings make their sails of wool; it takes a weaver a whole year to weave a big one."
msgstr ""
"I vichinghi fanno le vele di lana; a una tessitrice serve un anno intero per tesserne una grande."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey is the only sweet the vikings know, so the bees are worth a lot."
msgstr "Il miele è l'unico dolce che i vichinghi conoscono, perciò le api valgono molto."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "The runes are carved in straight lines, so that they are easy to cut in wood and stone."
msgstr "Le rune sono fatte di linee dritte, così è facile intagliarle nel legno e nella pietra."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "In winter, the lakes freeze, and people travel on skates made of horse bones."
msgstr "D'inverno i laghi gelano, e la gente viaggia su pattini fatti di ossa di cavallo."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "Women hold the keys of the house: a woman with keys on her belt runs the farm."
msgstr ""
"Le donne tengono le chiavi di casa: una donna con le chiavi alla cintura manda avanti la fattoria."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "The vikings give their boats names, like Long Serpent or Sea Horse."
msgstr "I vichinghi danno un nome alle loro barche, come Lungo Serpente o Cavallo di Mare."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cats on the farms catch the mice in the grain stores, so everybody loves them."
msgstr "I gatti delle fattorie acchiappano i topi nei granai, perciò tutti li adorano."

#. a fun fact of the viking times, which a skipper tells, at most 2 short sentences
#: scenes/game/gossip.gd
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good horse is worth more than a whole boatload of fish."
msgstr "Un buon cavallo vale più di una barca intera piena di pesce."

