#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese keeps the milk of the summer for the winter."
msgstr "Il formaggio conserva il latte dell'estate per l'inverno."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow of Our Own"
msgstr "Una mucca tutta nostra"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the east meadow, we have room for a cow at last! Buy one at the horse farm in Torsgården. A "
"cow is big, but she fits in your boat like a crate, if she stands still."
msgstr ""
"Con il prato a est, finalmente abbiamo posto per una mucca! {crew|Comprane|Comprane|Compratene} "
"una all'allevamento di cavalli di Torsgården. Una mucca è grande, ma nella barca sta come una "
"cassa, se sta ferma."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look at her big brown eyes! She will give us milk every day. Let us call her Rosa."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Guarda|Guarda|Guardate} che begli occhioni marroni! Ci darà il latte ogni giorno. "
"Chiamiamola Rosa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cows were the wealth of a farm: a family counted its riches in cows."
msgstr "Le mucche erano la ricchezza di una fattoria: una famiglia contava i suoi beni in mucche."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots for Ekvik"
msgstr "Vasi per Ekvik"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fish soup! We cook it for the whole village, but our big pot cracked. Bring us three crates of"
" pots from the potter, please."
msgstr ""
"La zuppa di pesce! La cuciniamo per tutto il villaggio, ma il nostro pentolone si è crepato. "
"{crew|Portaci|Portaci|Portateci} tre casse di vasi dalla vasaia, per favore."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New pots! Tonight there is fish soup for everybody, and for you two the first bowl."
msgstr ""
"Pentole nuove! Stasera c'è zuppa di pesce per tutti, e la prima scodella è per {crew|te|te|voi "
"due}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cooking pot hung over the fire on a chain, and the soup simmered all day."
msgstr "La pentola pendeva sul fuoco da una catena, e la zuppa sobbolliva tutto il giorno."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ragna's Broken Oar"
msgstr "Il remo rotto di Ragna"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ragna rowed out at dawn and is not back! I fear her oar broke. Find her on the lakes, then come "
"back and fetch the spare oar for her."
msgstr ""
"Ragna è uscita in barca all'alba e non è tornata! Temo che le si sia rotto il remo. "
"{crew|Trovala|Trovala|Trovatela} sui laghi, poi {crew|torna|torna|tornate} qui a prendere il remo "
"di scorta per lei."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hello! Yes, my oar broke, and I drift with one. Tell Tor to give you the spare one!"
msgstr ""
"Ciao! Sì, il mio remo si è rotto, e vado alla deriva con uno solo. {crew|Di'|Di'|Dite} a Tor di "
"{crew|darti|darti|darvi} quello di scorta!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "She is well? Thank the gods. Here is the oar: bring it to her!"
msgstr "Sta bene? Grazie agli dei. Ecco il remo: {crew|portaglielo|portaglielo|portateglielo}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My oar! Now I can row again. Here, take some fish: the freshest on the lakes."
msgstr ""
"Il mio remo! Ora posso remare di nuovo. Ecco, {crew|prendi|prendi|prendete} un po' di pesce: il "
"più fresco dei laghi."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every viking boat carried spare oars: a broken oar was common."
msgstr "Ogni barca vichinga portava remi di scorta: un remo rotto capitava spesso."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Torches for the Dark"
msgstr "Torce per il buio"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The nights grow long. The guests of the autumn feast need light: bring me tar for torches, two "
"pots from Ekvik, and two crates of flax for the wicks."
msgstr ""
"Le notti si allungano. Gli ospiti della festa d'autunno hanno bisogno di luce: "
"{crew|portami|portami|portatemi} catrame per le torce, due vasi da Ekvik, e due casse di lino per "
"gli stoppini."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar for torches? They burn bright and long."
msgstr "Catrame per le torce? Bruciano luminose e a lungo."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar and flax: now my torches will light up the whole bay!"
msgstr "Catrame e lino: ora le mie torce illumineranno tutta la baia!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking torches were sticks wrapped in flax or cloth, soaked in tar or fat."
msgstr ""
"Le torce vichinghe erano bastoni avvolti nel lino o nella stoffa, imbevuti di catrame o di grasso."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Autumn Feast"
msgstr "La festa d'autunno"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The autumn feast is tomorrow! Knut's ale is ready, five barrels. Bring them from Lindtorp, and "
"bring three crates of fish for the soup too."
msgstr ""
"Domani c'è la festa d'autunno! La birra di Knut è pronta, cinque barili. "
"{crew|Portali|Portali|Portateli} da Lindtorp, e {crew|porta|porta|portate} anche tre casse di "
"pesce per la zuppa."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ale! Now the fish."
msgstr "La birra! Ora il pesce."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The biggest batch I ever brewed! Five barrels for Orm."
msgstr "La birra più abbondante che abbia mai fatto! Cinque barili per Orm."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale, soup, torches, Sten's flute and Hrafn's knives! Everybody is here. Dance with us!"
msgstr ""
"Birra, zuppa, torce, il flauto di Sten e i coltelli di Hrafn! Ci sono tutti. "
"{crew|Balla|Balla|Ballate} con noi!"

