#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Big news: a ship from the Long Lake will come, and the way between the lakes opens! Tell the "
"smith, the fishers of Stormvik and Orm in Hallvik. I tell the rest."
msgstr ""
"Grandi notizie: arriverà una nave dal Lago Lungo, e si apre la via tra i laghi! "
"{crew|Avvisa|Avvisa|Avvisate} il fabbro, i pescatori di Stormvik e Orm a Hallvik. Al resto penso "
"io."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ship from the Long Lake? They will want my iron!"
msgstr "Una nave dal Lago Lungo? Vorranno il mio ferro!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New lakes, new fish! Thank you for telling us."
msgstr "Nuovi laghi, nuovi pesci! Grazie di avercelo detto."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Guests from far away! I must brew more. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr "Ospiti da lontano! Devo fare altra birra. Grazie, {crew|ragazzo|ragazza|ragazzi|ragazze}!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The lakes of the north were joined by rivers and portages, where boats were dragged over land."
msgstr ""
"I laghi del nord erano uniti da fiumi e da passaggi dove le barche venivano trascinate via terra."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow for Grim"
msgstr "Una mucca per Grim"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I am old, and I would like fresh milk every morning. Bring me a cow from the horse farm. The swans"
" will be jealous!"
msgstr ""
"Sono vecchio, e vorrei latte fresco ogni mattina. {crew|Portami|Portami|Portatemi} una mucca "
"dall'allevamento di cavalli. I cigni saranno gelosi!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A cow! I call her Swan, ha. Here, for your trouble, and for all the years you visited an old man."
msgstr ""
"Una mucca! La chiamo Cigno, ah. Ecco, per il disturbo, e per tutti gli anni in cui {crew|sei "
"venuto|sei venuta|siete venuti|siete venute} a trovare un vecchio."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good cow gave milk for ten years or more, and was part of the family."
msgstr "Una buona mucca dava latte per dieci anni o più, e faceva parte della famiglia."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flowers on the Hill"
msgstr "Fiori sulla collina"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plant flowers on the sunny hill! When they bloom, bring three crates to Gudrun's inn: she wants "
"the inn to smell like summer."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Semina|Semina|Seminate} fiori sulla collina al sole! Quando fioriscono, "
"{crew|portane|portane|portatene} tre casse alla locanda di Gudrun: vuole che la locanda profumi "
"d'estate."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flower seeds in the earth. In two days, they bloom."
msgstr "Semi di fiori nella terra. Tra due giorni fioriscono."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Flowers on every table! The guests smile. Here is your silver, and a cup of milk for each of you."
msgstr ""
"Fiori su ogni tavolo! Gli ospiti sorridono. Ecco il {crew|tuo|tuo|vostro} argento, e una tazza di "
"latte {crew|per te|per te|per ciascuno di voi}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings wove flowers into wreaths and crowns for feasts and weddings."
msgstr "I vichinghi intrecciavano fiori in ghirlande e corone per feste e matrimoni."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pottery Market"
msgstr "Il mercato dei vasi"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The new kiln makes so many pots! Bring ten crates to the market in Kråkhamn. Ten crates: only your"
" big boat can do it."
msgstr ""
"Il forno nuovo fa tantissimi vasi! {crew|Portane|Portane|Portatene} dieci casse al mercato di "
"Kråkhamn. Dieci casse: solo la {crew|tua|tua|vostra} barca grande ce la fa."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ten crates of Dagny's pots, and not one broken! The best rowing of the lakes."
msgstr "Dieci casse di vasi di Dagny, e neanche uno rotto! Il miglior remare dei laghi."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pack them in straw: pots do not like to bump!"
msgstr "{crew|Mettili|Mettili|Metteteli} nella paglia: ai vasi non piace sbattere!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
