#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Edge of the Forest"
msgstr "Il bordo del bosco"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kol and Ingrid want sheep for their new home. Bring them two sheep, and I give you the strip of "
"land by the forest, next to your farm. A fair trade!"
msgstr ""
"Kol e Ingrid vogliono pecore per la loro casa nuova. {crew|Portagli|Portagli|Portategli} due "
"pecore, e {crew|ti|ti|vi} do la striscia di terra vicino al bosco, accanto alla "
"{crew|tua|tua|vostra} fattoria. Uno scambio giusto!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two sheep for the young ones! Ingrid already knits. The forest edge is yours: good wood and two "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"Due pecore per i giovani sposi! Ingrid sta già lavorando a maglia. Il bordo del bosco è "
"{crew|tuo|tuo|vostro}: buona legna e due campi."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Land was traded for animals, silver or work: there were no banks."
msgstr "La terra si scambiava con animali, argento o lavoro: non c'erano banche."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Longhouse Grows"
msgstr "La casa lunga cresce"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"Con tanti animali e amici, la nostra casa è troppo piccola! {crew|Porta|Porta|Portate} dodici "
"tronchi da Frosttorp, due casse di attrezzi e due vasi di catrame, e la allunghiamo."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "Dodici tronchi! {crew|Riempi|Riempi|Riempite} quella {crew|tua|tua|vostra} grande stiva."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "Asce e chiodi. Ora il catrame per il tetto."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr ""
"Martellate tutta la notte con i vicini... La nostra casa lunga è lunga il doppio! C'è posto per "
"una festa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr "Una casa lunga si poteva allungare aggiungendo un pezzo in fondo, come un treno."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "La valle verde"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Hai|Hai|Avete} aiutato la mia valle tutto l'anno. La valle verde dietro la "
"{crew|tua|tua|vostra} fattoria non ha padrone: {crew|portami|portami|portatemi} due casse di "
"stoffa e due di miele per la festa degli dei, ed è {crew|tua|tua|vostra}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "Stoffa per la sala. Ora il miele."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "Papà lo dice al Thing, davanti a tutti: la valle verde appartiene a Ylva e Sigrid!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "Al Thing, l'assemblea degli uomini e delle donne liberi, si decidevano le terre e le leggi."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "Api per la valle"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"La valle è piena di trifoglio e di erica. Alle api piacerebbe tanto! {crew|Tieni|Tieni|Tenete} tre"
" arnie nella fattoria, e avremo miele tutto l'anno."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hum, hum, hum! Three hives in the valley. Honey for us, and for mead."
msgstr "Zzz, zzz, zzz! Tre arnie nella valle. Miele per noi, e per l'idromele."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Heather honey is dark and strong; clover honey is light and mild."
msgstr "Il miele di erica è scuro e forte; il miele di trifoglio è chiaro e delicato."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples for the Market"
msgstr "Mele per il mercato"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Thanks to the bees, my trees are full of apples! Twelve baskets for the market in Kråkhamn. Only "
"your boat can take them all at once."
msgstr ""
"Grazie alle api, i miei alberi sono pieni di mele! Dodici cesti per il mercato di Kråkhamn. Solo "
"la {crew|tua|tua|vostra} barca può portarli tutti in una volta."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve baskets of apples! The whole market smells of autumn."
msgstr "Dodici cesti di mele! Tutto il mercato profuma d'autunno."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Red and green and yellow. Take one for the trip!"
msgstr "Rosse, verdi e gialle. {crew|Prendine|Prendine|Prendetene} una per il viaggio!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
